Relevant columns and their potential usage  

• Track.TrackId: join key to InvoiceLine, identifier of each track  
• Track.Name: show human‑readable track title while exploring the data  
• Track.Milliseconds: original length of a track (in ms) –‑ convert to minutes, decide “Short / Medium / Long”  
• InvoiceLine.TrackId: connects each sale line to the corresponding Track  
• InvoiceLine.UnitPrice: price paid per unit of the track  
• InvoiceLine.Quantity: number of units sold –‑ use UnitPrice × Quantity to get revenue  

Typical conditions that may be used  

• JOIN "Track" t   ON  t.TrackId = il.TrackId –‑ to bring together duration and revenue  
• CASE  
     WHEN Milliseconds < 180000  THEN 'Short'             -- < 3 minutes  
     WHEN Milliseconds ≤ 300000 THEN 'Medium'            -- 3‑5 minutes  
     ELSE                               'Long'            -- > 5 minutes  
  END AS Category                                             

10 exploratory → final SQLite queries (each limited to 20 rows)  
```sql
-- 1. Inspect some raw lengths (milliseconds) that exist in Track
SELECT DISTINCT "Milliseconds"
FROM "Track"
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 2. Show first 20 tracks with their length already converted to minutes
SELECT "TrackId",
       "Name",
       ROUND("Milliseconds" / 60000.0, 2) AS "Minutes"
FROM "Track"
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 3. Classify the first 20 tracks as Short / Medium / Long using the chosen thresholds
SELECT "TrackId",
       "Name",
       "Milliseconds",
       CASE
           WHEN "Milliseconds" < 180000  THEN 'Short'
           WHEN "Milliseconds" <= 300000 THEN 'Medium'
           ELSE                               'Long'
       END AS "Category"
FROM "Track"
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 4. Count how many tracks fall into every category
SELECT CASE
           WHEN "Milliseconds" < 180000  THEN 'Short'
           WHEN "Milliseconds" <= 300000 THEN 'Medium'
           ELSE                               'Long'
       END AS "Category",
       COUNT(*) AS "Track_Count"
FROM "Track"
GROUP BY "Category"
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 5. Peek at sales data linked to tracks (first 20 joined rows)
SELECT il."InvoiceLineId",
       il."TrackId",
       t."Name",
       il."UnitPrice",
       il."Quantity"
FROM "InvoiceLine"  il
JOIN "Track"        t ON t."TrackId" = il."TrackId"
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 6. Revenue generated by each individual track (top 20 by revenue)
SELECT il."TrackId",
       t."Name",
       ROUND(SUM(il."UnitPrice" * il."Quantity"), 2) AS "Revenue"
FROM "InvoiceLine" il
JOIN "Track"       t ON t."TrackId" = il."TrackId"
GROUP BY il."TrackId"
ORDER BY "Revenue" DESC
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 7. Aggregate revenue per category
SELECT CASE
           WHEN t."Milliseconds" < 180000  THEN 'Short'
           WHEN t."Milliseconds" <= 300000 THEN 'Medium'
           ELSE                               'Long'
       END AS "Category",
       ROUND(SUM(il."UnitPrice" * il."Quantity"), 2) AS "Revenue"
FROM "InvoiceLine" il
JOIN "Track"       t ON t."TrackId" = il."TrackId"
GROUP BY "Category"
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 8. Minimum and maximum length (ms) for each category
SELECT CASE
           WHEN "Milliseconds" < 180000  THEN 'Short'
           WHEN "Milliseconds" <= 300000 THEN 'Medium'
           ELSE                               'Long'
       END AS "Category",
       MIN("Milliseconds") AS "Min_ms",
       MAX("Milliseconds") AS "Max_ms"
FROM "Track"
GROUP BY "Category"
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 9. Same as above but expressed in minutes, rounded to two decimals
SELECT CASE
           WHEN "Milliseconds" < 180000  THEN 'Short'
           WHEN "Milliseconds" <= 300000 THEN 'Medium'
           ELSE                               'Long'
       END AS "Category",
       ROUND(MIN("Milliseconds") / 60000.0, 2) AS "Min_Minutes",
       ROUND(MAX("Milliseconds") / 60000.0, 2) AS "Max_Minutes"
FROM "Track"
GROUP BY "Category"
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 10. FINAL ANSWER:  min & max time (minutes) and total revenue per Short / Medium / Long category
SELECT Category,
       ROUND(MIN_MS / 60000.0, 2) AS Min_Minutes,
       ROUND(MAX_MS / 60000.0, 2) AS Max_Minutes,
       ROUND(Total_Revenue, 2)    AS Total_Revenue
FROM (
    SELECT  CASE
                WHEN t."Milliseconds" < 180000  THEN 'Short'
                WHEN t."Milliseconds" <= 300000 THEN 'Medium'
                ELSE                               'Long'
            END                            AS Category,
            MIN(t."Milliseconds")          AS MIN_MS,
            MAX(t."Milliseconds")          AS MAX_MS,
            SUM(il."UnitPrice" * il."Quantity") AS Total_Revenue
    FROM  "Track"        t
    JOIN  "InvoiceLine"  il ON il."TrackId" = t."TrackId"
    GROUP BY Category
)
LIMIT 20;
```
